course: dictionary
lesson: 12733
title: Drinkable water and drinks
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Drinkable means safe enough to drink. The ending -able means "can be", so drinkable means "can be drunk". «The stream water was not drinkable, so we boiled it first.» The water could make us ill, so it had to be made safe.
explain: Drinkable has a second meaning, about taste. «The tea had gone cold, but it was still drinkable.» Nobody is ill here. The tea is simply pleasant enough to drink, not too hot, sour or strong.
explain: Use the clues around the word. Words like boiled, filtered or survival tell you the meaning is about safety. Words like cold, sour or strong tell you the meaning is about taste. Then swap in "safe to drink" or "pleasant enough to drink" and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Drinkable means safe to drink.
fact: «Drinkable» can also mean pleasant enough to drink, not too hot, sour or strong.
fact: The ending -able means "can be", so drinkable means "can be drunk".
fact: «Not drinkable» means the water is not safe, so you must not drink it.
fact: In survival stories, people search for drinkable water, and they may filter or boil water to make it drinkable.
exercise: «The river water looked clear, but it was not drinkable.» What does drinkable mean here? | Good for washing your hands | Cold and fresh from the mountains | Full of fish | *Safe to drink
exercise: «Mum said the lemonade was too sour, but it was still drinkable.» What does drinkable mean here? | *Just pleasant enough to drink | Made in a factory | Hot enough to burn your mouth
exercise: Which phrase means the water is safe to drink? | *Make the water drinkable | Make the water into a game | Make the water freeze solid | Make the water louder
test: «The explorers boiled the stream water to make it drinkable.» What does drinkable mean here? | Very warm to touch | Full of mud | Easy to swim in | *Safe to drink
test: «Dad said the coffee was drinkable, but he wanted it sweeter.» What does drinkable mean here? | *Pleasant enough to drink | Full of sugar | Dangerous to swallow | Frozen solid
exam: What does «not drinkable» mean in «After the flood, the village had no drinkable water»? | Water that is very cold | Too much water to carry | Water with too many fish | *No water that is safe to drink
